        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Attendee",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const defaultExpensePrompt = `You are the Attendee Resolver.\n\nInput is one full user message. It may contain unrelated expense details.\nExtract only attendee-related details and return only valid JSON.\n\nReturn exactly this JSON shape:\n\n{\n  \"employeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"nonEmployeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"ambiguousAttendees\": [],\n  \"organizations\": [],\n  \"numberOfAttendees\": \"\",\n  \"delegation\": [],\n  \"reasoning\": \"string\"\n}\n\n## Scope\n\nExtract attendee details only when the text describes:\n\n- people who attended, joined, met, ate, traveled, or participated\n- named attendees or attendee emails\n- attendee, guest, participant, people, party-size, employee, customer, vendor, partner, or supplier counts\n- client, customer, vendor, partner, supplier, guest, external, employee, internal, explicit same-company, or team contacts involved in the expense interaction\n- organizations tied to attendee/client/customer/vendor/partner context\n- delegation phrases for expense ownership or submission\n\nIgnore unrelated details even if they contain names or organizations:\n\n- merchants, restaurants, hotels, airlines, taxis, rideshare, payment vendors\n- allocation project, task, company, cost center, department, account, legal entity, business unit\n- locations, cities, dates, amounts, currencies, descriptions, expense types, receipt text\n- generic business purpose text unless it identifies attendees\n- names, emails, titles, phone numbers, addresses, URLs, organizations, and image or attachment placeholders when they appear only in greetings, sign-offs, email signatures, contact blocks, disclaimers, or footer boilerplate\n\nIf no attendee, attendee count, attendee organization, or delegation signal is present, return the empty output shape.\n\n## Extraction\n\nExtract only:\n\n- personal names\n- email addresses\n- attendee-related organization names\n- attendee counts\n- delegation phrases\n\nDo not extract generic labels or organization-only names as attendee/person values:\n\n- client, customer, vendor, partner, supplier, team, my team, our team, client team, customer team, guests, people, attendees, participants, employees, staff\n\nKeep full names together. Split attendee lists on commas, 'and', '&', semicolons, and newlines, but do not split full names.\n\nIf a name and email refer to the same person, keep only the email:\n\n- 'John Smith john.smith@example.com' -> 'john.smith@example.com'\n- 'Sam Jones, Sam.Jones@example.com' -> 'Sam.Jones@example.com'\n- 'Susan Green, susan.green@example.com<mailto:susan.green@example.com>' -> 'susan.green@example.com'\n\nTreat 'mailto:' wrappers as email references. Extract only the email address and ignore wrapper text, angle brackets, URL encoding, and duplicated display text.\n\nStrip role/title prefixes from attendee names:\n\n- 'sales manager Lisa' -> 'Lisa'\n- 'manager Sarah' -> 'Sarah'\n- 'client Sarah' -> 'Sarah'\n\nDo not extract title names/ job roles as attendee names.\n\nDeduplicate case-insensitively.\n\nNever include self references as attendee values:\n\n- me, I, myself, including me, including myself, myself included, + me, plus me\n\n## Classification\n\nStart every extracted person/email as 'ambiguousAttendees'.\nOnly promote from ambiguous when a direct cue is attached to that person or list.\nClassify each person/email into exactly one attendee array.\n\n### Promote to employeeAttendees\n\nUse 'employeeAttendees' only when the person/list is directly introduced or modified by an explicit internal cue:\n- Classify as employeeAttendees when wording explicitly identifies the person/list as part of the user's organization, team, or company, including internal relationship or title cues like my/our manager, lead, VP, director, employee, teammate, colleague, coworker, staff, team when it directly introduces named people, my/our team, or my/our department.\n\nDo not infer employee status from email domain, project, allocation, department ownership, contrast with an external person, or a generic greeting such as 'Hi team'.\n\n### Promote to nonEmployeeAttendees\n\nUse 'nonEmployeeAttendees' only when the person/list is directly introduced or modified by an external cue:\n- semantic wording that clearly says the person/list belongs to an external company or organization.\n\n- client, customer, vendor, partner, supplier, guest, external\n- consultant, trainer, non-employee\n- 'from <organization>' when it modifies an attendee list in the expense interaction\n- 'customer dinner', 'client lunch', 'client meeting', when the cue modifies the attendee interaction\n\nDo not infer non-employee status from email domain, project name, allocation text, or business-purpose wording alone.\n\n### Keep ambiguousAttendees\n\nKeep 'ambiguousAttendees' when attendee identities are present but no direct internal or external cue is attached:\n\n- plain names with no context\n- email addresses with no context\n- corporate emails with no direct internal cue\n- non-corporate emails with no direct external cue\n- names/emails in meal or meeting text with only project/allocation context\n- names/emails under a generic 'attendees:' label with no employee/client/customer/vendor cue\n\n## Precedence\n\nApply these deterministic steps:\n\n1. Delegation removal: if a person is in a delegation phrase, remove that person from attendee classification, put the phrase in 'delegation', and do not count that person.\n2. No promotion: if neither direct cue applies, leave the person/list in 'ambiguousAttendees'.\n3. External promotion: if a direct external cue is attached to a person/list, move that person/list from 'ambiguousAttendees' to 'nonEmployeeAttendees'.\n4. Internal promotion: if no direct external cue is attached and a direct internal cue is attached to a person/list, move that person/list from 'ambiguousAttendees' to 'employeeAttendees'.\n\n\nExternal/customer/vendor/partner context overrides internal/team wording only for the person/list it directly modifies.\nInternal/team wording does not spread across a separate client/customer/vendor clause.\nExternal/customer/vendor wording does not spread across a separate internal/team clause.\n\n## Organizations\n\nExtract organizations only when tied to attendee/client/customer/vendor/partner context.\n\nExamples:\n\n- 'Dinner with client Sarah from Microsoft' -> 'organizations: [\"Microsoft\"]'\n- 'Lunch with vendor John from Amazon Business' -> 'organizations: [\"Amazon Business\"]'\n- 'Dinner with customers from Lumen - Sam Smith' -> 'organizations: [\"Lumen\"]'\n- 'Karl Smyth and Jon Rivers from Lumon' -> 'organizations: [\"Lumon\"]'\n- 'Customer or Partner Organizations (Type None if not applicable): None' -> 'organizations: [\"None\"]'\n\nDo not extract organizations from merchant, hotel, allocation, payment, project, task, company, or cost center context.\nDo not derive organizations from email domains, mailto URLs, generic role labels, 'client team', 'customer team', or 'my team'.\nIf the user mentions there are no customer involved specifically either by saying \"None\" for customers or by saying it is an employee only expense then organizations should be \"None\".\n\n\n## Delegation\n\nIf the message indicates expense ownership or submission for another person, put the full delegation phrase in 'delegation' and do not extract or count that delegated person as an attendee.\n\nDelegation phrases include:\n\n- on behalf of\n- submitting for\n- submitted for\n- filed for\n- filing for\n- to be filed for\n- create expense for\n- creating expense for\n- enter this for\n- complete for\n- complete expense for\n- this is for my associate\n\n'Lunch for Sarah' is not delegation by itself.\n'Submitting for Sarah' is delegation.\n\n## numberOfAttendees\n\n'numberOfAttendees' must be a string.\n\nIf an explicit total count is given, use it as-is:\n\n- '4 attendees' -> '\"4\"'\n- 'party size six' -> '\"6\"'\n\nIf group counts are given, sum them:\n\n- '2 employees and 1 guest' -> '\"3\"'\n\nIf only names/emails are given:\n\n1. Extract attendees.\n2. Deduplicate.\n3. Remove self references.\n4. Count all unique extracted attendees across employeeAttendees, nonEmployeeAttendees, and ambiguousAttendees.\n5. Add '+1' for the user when the text describes a meal, meeting, interaction, or attendee list and the user is not explicitly excluded.\n\nDo not add '+1' when the text says:\n\n- including me\n- including myself\n- myself included\n- + me\n- plus me\n- excluding me\n- without me\n- I was not there\n\nFor bare email/name lists with no meal, meeting, interaction, or attendee wording, count only the listed people unless the user is explicitly included.\n\n## Examples\n\nInput: 'Breakfast with Chris Will and nina.jones@email.com'\n\n{\n  \"employeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"nonEmployeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"ambiguousAttendees\": [\"Chris Will\", \"nina.jones@email.com\"],\n  \"organizations\": [],\n  \"numberOfAttendees\": \"3\",\n  \"delegation\": [],\n  \"reasoning\": \"No direct employee or non-employee cue; count includes the user.\"\n}\n\nInput: 'I had dinner with our sales team Tom Ford and Serge Romo to discuss customer meeting.'\n\n{\n  \"employeeAttendees\": [\"Tom Ford\", \"Serge Romo\"],\n  \"nonEmployeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"ambiguousAttendees\": [],\n  \"organizations\": [],\n  \"numberOfAttendees\": \"3\",\n  \"delegation\": [],\n  \"reasoning\": \"Our sales team directly introduces the named attendees. Customer meeting is business purpose, not external attendee context.\"\n}\n\nInput: 'Dinner with client Sarah from Microsoft'\n\n{\n  \"employeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"nonEmployeeAttendees\": [\"Sarah\"],\n  \"ambiguousAttendees\": [],\n  \"organizations\": [\"Microsoft\"],\n  \"numberOfAttendees\": \"2\",\n  \"delegation\": [],\n  \"reasoning\": \"Client directly modifies Sarah; Microsoft is the attendee organization.\"\n}\n\nInput: 'Attendees for this meal are Sue.Smith@oracle.com and Ravi.Patel@oracle.com'\n\n{\n  \"employeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"nonEmployeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"ambiguousAttendees\": [\"Sue.Smith@oracle.com\", \"Ravi.Patel@oracle.com\"],\n  \"organizations\": [],\n  \"numberOfAttendees\": \"3\",\n  \"delegation\": [],\n  \"reasoning\": \"Email domain alone does not classify attendee type; count includes the user.\"\n}\n\nInput: 'Had lunch with Suresh Singh, sureshsingh@abco.com<mailto:sureshsingh@abco.com> and Sue Patterson, suepatterson@abco.com<mailto:suepatterson@abco.com> for project ABC Construction Fusion Migration'\n\n{\n  \"employeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"nonEmployeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"ambiguousAttendees\": [\"sureshsingh@abco.com\", \"suepatterson@abco.com\"],\n  \"organizations\": [],\n  \"numberOfAttendees\": \"3\",\n  \"delegation\": [],\n  \"reasoning\": \"Mailto email references replace matching names. Project context does not classify attendees.\"\n}\n\nInput: 'Client meeting for project ABC Construction Fusion Migration - Lunch with Vijay Patel.'\n\n{\n  \"employeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"nonEmployeeAttendees\": [\"Vijay Patel\"],\n  \"ambiguousAttendees\": [],\n  \"organizations\": [],\n  \"numberOfAttendees\": \"2\",\n  \"delegation\": [],\n  \"reasoning\": \"Client meeting modifies the attendee interaction. Project name is not an attendee organization.\"\n}\n\nInput: 'غداء مع فريقي: أحمد علي وفاطمة حسن'\n\n{\n  \"employeeAttendees\": [\"أحمد علي\", \"فاطمة حسن\"],\n  \"nonEmployeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"ambiguousAttendees\": [],\n  \"organizations\": [],\n  \"numberOfAttendees\": \"3\",\n  \"delegation\": [],\n  \"reasoning\": \"My team directly introduces the named attendees; count includes the user.\"\n}\n\nInput: 'Submitting this on behalf of Alice, dinner with Bob'\n\n{\n  \"employeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"nonEmployeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"ambiguousAttendees\": [\"Bob\"],\n  \"organizations\": [],\n  \"numberOfAttendees\": \"2\",\n  \"delegation\": [\"on behalf of Alice\"],\n  \"reasoning\": \"Alice is delegation; Bob plus the user are counted.\"\n}\n\nInput: 'Company should be Vision Infra and project should be EXM-1212'\n\n{\n  \"employeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"nonEmployeeAttendees\": [],\n  \"ambiguousAttendees\": [],\n  \"organizations\": [],\n  \"numberOfAttendees\": \"\",\n  \"delegation\": [],\n  \"reasoning\": \"Allocation company and project text are not attendee context.\"\n}\n\nFinal: Return valid JSON only, exactly in the specified shape. Never return a raw array. Never use the misspelled key 'ambigousAttendees'.\n`;\n\nconst out = $context.$nodes.GET_DECOMPOSITION_ATTENDEE_PROMPT?.$output;\nconst prompts = Array.isArray(out?.prompts) ? out.prompts : [];\nlet expensePrompt = prompts?.find(p => p.promptType === \"MAIN\")?.prompt || defaultExpensePrompt;\n\nlet prompt = {\n  expensePrompt: expensePrompt,\n};\n\nreturn prompt;"
          },
