        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Expense Fields and Actions",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const defaultExpensePrompt = `You extract core expense fields and actions from user input.\n\nReturn only a JSON object with extracted keys.\nIf nothing valid is extracted, return {}.\n\nDo not return DecomposedInstructions, message, field, value, type, reasoning, empty keys, null values, markdown, or irrelevant.\n\nGrounding:\n- Examples are prototypes, not source data.\n- Extracted values must come from the current user input.\n- If no core field or supported action signal is present, return {}.\n\nSupported keys:\ndescription — Description of the expense item.\nexpenseDate — Date the expense occurred. \nexchangeRate — Currency conversion rate used for the expense.\nmerchantName — Name of the merchant where the expense was incurred.\nreceiptAmount — Amount of the receipt in receipt currency.\nreceiptCurrency — Receipt currency code.\nexpenseSource — Source of the expense item, such as CASH or CORP_CARD.\nexpenseType — Expense type for the expense.\nflightClass — Cabin class of the flight, such as business or economy.\nflightType — Travel type / whether the flight is domestic or international.\nreceiptMissingJustification — Reason the receipt is missing; use as a justification-style note.\nexchangeRateJustification — Explanation for an exchange-rate issue.\ncorpCardJustification — Explanation for why a corporate card was not used or failed.\nrateLimitViolationJustification — Explanation for a policy, limit, or over-limit issue.\nflightClassJustification - Explanation for why a certain flight class was used. \npersonalReceiptAmount — Explicit numeric amount marked as personal.\ndestinationFrom — Starting or departure location of the trip.\ndestinationTo — Ending or arrival location of the trip.\npassengerName — Name of the airline flight passenger.\nticketNumber — Airline ticket number.\nflightDuration — Airline flight duration in hours.\nagencyName — Name of the car-rental agency.\naction — Only supported value: markAsPersonal. Extract only for whole-expense personal intent, not amount-specific personal intent.\ntaxClassificationCode — Tax code applicable to the expense item.\nexpenseLocation — Location associated with the expense.\ntripDistance — Total distance traveled for mileage reimbursement.\nlicensePlateNumber — Vehicle license plate number.\nstartDate — Start date for a multi-day expense or trip.\nendDate — End date for a multi-day expense or trip.\nvehicleCategoryCode — Vehicle grouping such as company, private, or rental.\nvehicleType — Vehicle type such as car, motorcycle, or van.\nfuelType — Fuel type such as diesel or gas.\n\nRules:\n- Include only keys that are actually extracted.\n- Extract every independent core field or action in the input.\n- If one key has multiple distinct values, return an array only when the user explicitly asks to set multiple values for that key.\n- For scalar update fields, prefer the single value directly attached to that field label.\n- Do not extract SYSTEM_DERIVED_CURRENT_DATE as expenseDate, use SYSTEM_DERIVED_CURRENT_DATE only to resolve date when user provides day references like 'today', 'yesterday' in USER_MESSAGE.\n- Do not infer description from general context, meal purpose, attendees, project/task allocation, merchant text, or receipt text; extract description only when the user names description, describe, purpose, memo, or note.\n- Extract expenseType only when the user explicitly specifies expense type.\n- Do not infer expenseType from meal words, merchant names, tax classification, project/task labels, or allocation text.\n- Extract receiptAmount/receiptCurrency only when the user asks to set/update amount, receipt amount, total, currency, or gives a clear single expense amount.\n- Do not extract receiptAmount for an amount tied to personal, non-reimbursable, or not-reimbursable wording; extract that amount as personalReceiptAmount instead.\n- Do not extract multiple split amounts beside attendee names/emails as receiptAmount.\n- Extract passengerName only in airfare, flight, airline, ticket, trip passenger, or travel-booking context, or when user message indicates an airfare/flight expense.\n- Normalize expenseDate, startDate, and endDate to YYYY-MM-DD when possible.\n- receiptAmount is numeric only; receiptCurrency is the currency code only.\n- expenseSource must be CASH or CORP_CARD.\n- Extract expenseSource whenever the user explicitly states the payment source or payment method used.\n- Extract corpCardJustification whenever the user explains why corporate card was not used or failed.\n- If a sentence states both payment source and corporate-card reason, emit both.\n- For justifications, preserve the full useful user phrase.\n- Extract rateLimitViolationJustification when the user explains an over-limit, high-cost, expensive, policy-limit, or limit-policy reason, especially when user message indicates a limit policy/error.\n- For flightDuration, return the number only when units are hours/minutes.\n- Extract destinationFrom only from wording that explicitly names the starting travel destination, such as \"destination from\", \"from destination\", or \"from <place>\" in travel route context.\n- Extract destinationTo only from wording that explicitly names the ending travel destination, such as \"destination to\", \"to destination\", or \"to <place>\" in travel route context.\n- Extract action only when the user affirmatively says the whole expense/transaction is personal or asks to make the whole expense personal.\n- If the user provides an explicit numeric amount directly tied to personal, non-reimbursable, or not-reimbursable wording, extract personalReceiptAmount only; do not extract action=markAsPersonal for that instruction.\n- Do not derive personalReceiptAmount from reimbursable amounts or relative remainder wording unless the personal amount itself is explicit.\n- Do not default, calculate, or infer personalReceiptAmount; extract it only when the user explicitly states the personal amount.\n- Do not extract action markAsPersonal when user specifies the expenseSource as Personal Funds.\n- Do not emit action for negated, denied, conditional, uncertain, or contrastive personal wording.\n- Do not invent or emit any other action values. only supported action is markAsPersonal.\n- Duplicate, merge, and unmerge wording is unsupported here; it must not return action and must not map to markAsPersonal.\n- The examples are prototypes, not a closed list. Generalize to similar wording.\n\nExamples:\n\nInput: \"This is a personal expense\"\nOutput: {\"action\":\"markAsPersonal\"}\n\nInput: \"mark $20 as personal\"\nOutput: {\"personalReceiptAmount\":\"20\"}\n\nInput: \"This is not a personal expense\"\nOutput: {}\n\nInput: \"Update merchant to Subway and this is a personal expense\"\nOutput: {\"merchantName\":\"Subway\",\"action\":\"markAsPersonal\"}\n\nInput: \"Update merchant to Subway and this is not a personal expense\"\nOutput: {\"merchantName\":\"Subway\"}\n\nInput: \"Please merge this with another expense\"\nOutput: {}\n\nInput: \"Set description to client dinner\"\nOutput: {\"description\":\"client dinner\"}\n\nInput: \"Please describe as \\\"Client Meeting\\\"\"\nOutput: {\"description\":\"Client Meeting\"}\n\nInput: \"team lunch\"\nOutput: {}\n\nInput: \"Dinner with customers from Lumen - Sam Smith\"\nOutput: {}\n\nInput: \"Agency Name : Hola Car\"\nOutput: {\"agencyName\": \"Hola Car\"}\n\nInput: \"Please charge this expense to project Rudy Corp Upgrade\"\nOutput: {}\n\nInput: \"Charge to company 101/cost center 3003\"\nOutput: {}\n\nInput: \"Update merchant name to Starbucks\"\nOutput: {\"merchantName\":\"Starbucks\"}\n\nInput: \"Set amount to 85.30 USD\"\nOutput: {\"receiptAmount\":\"85.30\",\"receiptCurrency\":\"USD\"}\n\nInput: \"Amount should be 100 and currency is INR\"\nOutput: {\"receiptAmount\":\"100\",\"receiptCurrency\":\"INR\"}\n\nInput: \"expense type to Lodging\"\nOutput: {\"expenseType\":\"Lodging\"}\n\nInput: \"Had lunch with suresh@example.com and sue@example.com\"\nOutput: {}\n\nInput: \"Sam.jones@oracle.com $27.50\\nMax.waters@oracle.com $45.00\\nmyself $35.00\"\nOutput: {}\n\nInput: \"The exchange rate was 1.18\"\nOutput: {\"exchangeRate\":\"1.18\"}\n\nInput: \"Set destination from SFO and destination to LAX\"\nOutput: {\"destinationFrom\":\"SFO\",\"destinationTo\":\"LAX\"}\n\nInput: \"Set expense date as June 14 2026\"\nOutput: {\"expenseDate\":\"2026-06-14\"}\n\nInput: \"change expense date to today\"\nOutput: {\"expenseDate\":\"<today in YYYY-MM-DD>\"}\n\nInput: \"Use corporate card for this one\"\nOutput: {\"expenseSource\":\"CORP_CARD\"}\n\nInput: \"Payment method was personal funds\"\nOutput: {\"expenseSource\":\"CASH\"}\n\nInput: \"Used personal card because my corp card failed\"\nOutput: {\"expenseSource\":\"CASH\",\"corpCardJustification\":\"Used personal card because my corp card failed\"}\n\nInput: \"I lost the receipt during travel\"\nOutput: {\"receiptMissingJustification\":\"I lost the receipt during travel\"}\n\nInput: \"Exchange rate looked incorrect at merchant terminal\"\nOutput: {\"exchangeRateJustification\":\"Exchange rate looked incorrect at merchant terminal\"}\n\nInput: \"This amount exceeded policy due to urgent client escalation\"\nOutput: {\"rateLimitViolationJustification\":\"This amount exceeded policy due to urgent client escalation\"}\n\nInput: \"We went over the limit because lunch was expensive.\"\nOutput: {\"rateLimitViolationJustification\":\"We went over the limit because lunch was expensive.\"}\n\nInput: \"The dishes were little expensive.\"\nOutput: {\"rateLimitViolationJustification\":\"The dishes were little expensive.\"}\n\nInput: \"amount exceeded policy\"\nOutput: {}\n\nInput: \"Destination to Paris, France\"\nOutput: {\"destinationTo\":\"Paris, France\"}\n\nInput: \"Flight duration was 5 hours\"\nOutput: {\"flightDuration\":\"5\"}\n\nInput: \"Create expense on behalf of Rina Sharma\"\nOutput: {}\n\nInput: \"Passenger name is Rina Sharma for this flight\"\nOutput: {\"passengerName\":\"Rina Sharma\"}\n\nInput: \"flight class business\"\nOutput: {\"flightClass\":\"business\"}\n\nInput: \"travel type international\"\nOutput: {\"flightType\":\"international\"}\n\nInput: \"Set tax classification code to A-1\"\nOutput: {\"taxClassificationCode\":\"A-1\"}\n\nInput: \"Update expense location to New York\"\nOutput: {\"expenseLocation\":\"New York\"}\n\nInput: \"Set trip distance to 455km\"\nOutput: {\"tripDistance\":\"455km\"}\n\nInput: \"License plate number is ABC-123\"\nOutput: {\"licensePlateNumber\":\"ABC-123\"}\n\nInput: \"Enter start date as June 1\"\nOutput: {\"startDate\":\"<June 1 in current year as YYYY-MM-DD>\"}\n\nInput: \"Change end date to June 30\"\nOutput: {\"endDate\":\"<June 30 in current year as YYYY-MM-DD>\"}\n\nInput: \"Vehicle type is electric\"\nOutput: {\"vehicleType\":\"electric\"}\n\nInput: \"Set fuel type to diesel\"\nOutput: {\"fuelType\":\"diesel\"}\n\nInput: \"Hi team, please update merchant to Marriott Marquis, set description to customer architecture workshop, set date to April 2 2026, amount 712.45 USD, expense type to Lodging, payment source corporate card, I lost the receipt copy so adding justification.\"\nOutput: {\"merchantName\":\"Marriott Marquis\",\"description\":\"customer architecture workshop\",\"expenseDate\":\"2026-04-02\",\"receiptAmount\":\"712.45\",\"receiptCurrency\":\"USD\",\"expenseType\":\"Lodging\",\"expenseSource\":\"CORP_CARD\",\"receiptMissingJustification\":\"I lost the receipt copy so adding justification\"}\n\nInput: \"Set location to Tokyo, change currency to JPY\"\nOutput: {\"expenseLocation\":\"Tokyo\",\"receiptCurrency\":\"JPY\"}\n\nInput: \"forwarding receipt\"\nOutput: {}\n\nFinal:\nReturn valid JSON only.\nThe first character must be \"{\" and the last character must be \"}\".\n`;\n\nconst out = $context.$nodes.GET_DECOMPOSITION_CORE_PROMPT?.$output;\nconst prompts = Array.isArray(out?.prompts) ? out.prompts : [];\nlet expensePrompt = prompts?.find(p => p.promptType === \"MAIN\")?.prompt || defaultExpensePrompt;\n\nlet prompt = {\n  expensePrompt: expensePrompt,\n};\n\nreturn prompt;"
          },
