          "code": "GET_DECOMPOSITION_RECOMMENDATION_PROMPT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1778998251047",
          "id": "1777538720539",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777538747696_1",
              "name": "agentName",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "DECOMPOSITION_RECOMMENDATION"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Recommendation Option Selector",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const defaultExpensePrompt = `You are the Recommendation Option Selector.\n\nTask: From the user's reply, select existing recommendation options from projectedOptionsVar and separate any remaining non-option instruction text. Return only options that are clearly chosen. If nothing clearly maps to an existing option, return an empty selection array and keep the full user reply as additionalMessage.\n\nInputs:\n- recommendationClauses = recommendationClausesVar. This may be the full user message.\n- projectedOptions = projectedOptionsVar. These are compact views of the real options.\n\nReturn only JSON:\n{\n  \"recommendedOptionSelections\": [],\n  \"additionalMessage\": \"\"\n}\n\nFor each selected option:\n{\n  \"sentence\": \"<exact user reply fragment that selected the option>\",\n  \"selectedOptionKey\": \"<matched projectedOptions.optionKey>\",\n  \"selectedOptionId\": \"<matched projectedOptions.id, if present>\",\n  \"predictionString\": \"<option number or matched value text>\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"<short reason>\"\n}\n\nRules:\n1. Select only from projectedOptions. Never invent an option.\n2. Do not output fieldValue or fieldType. Downstream code will hydrate those from the matched option.\n3. Process every independent reply fragment. Split on new lines, semicolons, and repeated patterns like \"<label>: Option <n>\".\n4. Ignore quoted email headers, signatures, and instruction-only text. If a line has instruction text followed by a colon, use only the text after the last colon as the user's option answer, but keep any separate non-option instruction text in additionalMessage.\n5. selectedOptionKey must exactly match the chosen projectedOptions.optionKey.\n6. additionalMessage must contain only remaining user-authored instructions that should still be decomposed by other resolvers. Remove option-only fragments, prompt text, labels that merely ask the user to choose, and selected option tokens.\n7. If at least one recommendation is selected and no remaining instruction text exists, additionalMessage must be \"\".\n8. If no recommendation is selected, additionalMessage must be the original recommendationClauses text, trimmed.\n\nA reply fragment can select an option in these ways:\n\nA. Option number\n- \"1\", \"2\", \"3\"\n- \"Option 1\", \"option 2\"\n- \"first option\", \"second option\", \"third option\"\n- \"I choose 2\", \"select option 3\"\n\nMatch number selections to projectedOption.predictionRank first. If that fails, match projectedOption.driverValue1 or projectedOption.driverValue2. If a field label is present, restrict to that field family before matching.\n\nB. Value text\nThe user may reply with the option value instead of a number, and the value may be partial:\n- \"ABC project\"\n- \"Finance cost center\"\n- \"Vision Operations\"\n- \"John Smith\"\n- \"john.smith@example.com\"\n- \"SA-1001\" or \"conference preapproval\"\n\nMatch value text against projectedOption.driverValue1, projectedOption.driverValue2, and projectedOption.searchText. A partial match is valid only when it uniquely identifies one option within the relevant field family. If multiple options match, output nothing for that fragment.\n\nC. Attendee disambiguation\nFor fragments like \"Which David attended: Option 1\" or \"David: 2\":\n- First match the person name/email against attendee-related projected options.\n- Then match the option number within that person's options.\n- Output one item for each matched person-option pair.\n- Treat the whole disambiguation prompt plus option answer as option-selection text, not additionalMessage.\n\nD. Attendee value reply\nFor fragments like \"John and Sarah attended\", match each name/email to attendee-related projected options. Output one item per uniquely matched attendee. If a name/email is not unique, skip that name/email.\n\nOverride rule:\nIf a fragment contains an option number plus a same-field correction such as \"but\", \"instead\", \"not\", \"wrong\", \"use\", \"set\", \"change\", or \"update\", do not use the option number. Try to match the corrected value text to an existing projected option. If it uniquely matches, output that matched option. If it does not uniquely match, output nothing for that field.\n\nExamples:\n- \"Option 1, but use project ABC instead\" -> ignore Option 1; select ABC only if ABC uniquely matches a Project option.\n- \"Option 2 is wrong, use Finance\" -> ignore Option 2; select Finance only if it uniquely matches the same field family.\n- \"Accounts: Option 1, and use project ABC\" -> select Accounts Option 1; leave project ABC in additionalMessage only if it is not itself selected as a recommendation option.\n- \"Enter option 1 or 2, or enter which Lisa Williams attended: Option 2\" -> selected option only, additionalMessage \"\".\n- \"Option 2; amount is 45 and description is client dinner\" -> selected option plus additionalMessage \"amount is 45 and description is client dinner\".\n\nField family hints:\n- Project, Projects, Task, Tasks, Project and Task -> Project-related options\n- Account, Accounts, Company, Cost Center, Cost Centre -> Company or Cost Center options, based on projectedOption.fieldName\n- Attendee, Attendees, Who attended, Which <person> attended -> Attendee options\n- Spend Authorization, Spend Authorization Line, Authorization, Preapproval, Spend Auth -> spend authorization options\n\nFinal checks:\n- Return every clear match; do not stop after the first.\n- Do not output duplicate matches.\n- Do not guess when a number or value can match multiple options.\n- Output valid JSON only.`;\n\nconst out = $context.$nodes.GET_DECOMPOSITION_RECOMMENDATION_PROMPT?.$output;\nconst prompts = Array.isArray(out?.prompts) ? out.prompts : [];\nlet expensePrompt = prompts?.find(p => p.promptType === \"MAIN\")?.prompt || defaultExpensePrompt;\n\nlet prompt = {\n  expensePrompt: expensePrompt,\n};\n\nreturn prompt;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778998422914"
          },
          "code": "RECOMMENDATION_OPTION_SELECTOR",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1778998251047",
          "id": "1777539338416",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Project Recommendation Options",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "var optionsVar = $context.$variables.options || {};\nvar optionItems = [];\n\nif (optionsVar.options && optionsVar.options.items && optionsVar.options.items.length >= 0) {\n  optionItems = optionsVar.options.items;\n} else if (optionsVar.items && optionsVar.items.length >= 0) {\n  optionItems = optionsVar.items;\n}\n\nvar projectedOptions = [];\n\nfor (var i = 0; i < optionItems.length; i++) {\n  var option = optionItems[i] || {};\n  var projected = {};\n\n  projected.optionKey = \"opt_\" + i;\n  projected.id = option.id || \"\";\n  projected.fieldName = option.fieldName || \"\";\n  projected.predictionRank = option.predictionRank || \"\";\n  projected.driverValue1 = option.driverValue1 || \"\";\n  projected.driverValue2 = option.driverValue2 || \"\";\n\n  var searchText = \"\";\n\n  if (projected.fieldName) searchText = searchText + projected.fieldName + \" \";\n  if (projected.predictionRank) searchText = searchText + projected.predictionRank + \" \";\n  if (projected.driverValue1) searchText = searchText + projected.driverValue1 + \" \";\n  if (projected.driverValue2) searchText = searchText + projected.driverValue2 + \" \";\n  if (projected.id) searchText = searchText + projected.id + \" \";\n  if (option.fieldValue) searchText = searchText + option.fieldValue;\n\n  projected.searchText = searchText;\n  projectedOptions[projectedOptions.length] = projected;\n}\n\nreturn { projectedOptions: projectedOptions };"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778998251047"
          },
          "code": "PROJECT_RECOMMENDATION_OPTIONS",
          "id": "1778998422914",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
